# ============================================================================
# Majlis — database/.gitignore
# Keep the SECRET, the BACKUP, and transient SQLite sidecars OUT of version
# control. NEVER commit the passphrase or anything derived from it.
# ============================================================================

# --- the SQLCipher passphrase: NEVER commit, in any form --------------------
# (We never write the key to a file, but block the usual leak vectors anyway.)
.env
.env.*
*.key
*.secret
secrets.*
*passphrase*
*MAJLIS_DB_KEY*

# --- plaintext backup left behind by encrypt_db.sh --------------------------
# This is unencrypted data — must never reach the repo. Securely delete it
# locally once the encrypted DB is verified.
knowledge.plaintext.bak
*.plaintext.bak

# --- transient migration artifact -------------------------------------------
knowledge.encrypted.db
knowledge.encrypted.db-wal
knowledge.encrypted.db-shm

# --- SQLite WAL / SHM sidecars (regenerated at runtime) ---------------------
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
*-wal
*-shm

# --- dedicated Python venv (source-built sqlcipher3 binding, machine-local) --
# Large, platform-specific, and rebuildable — never commit it.
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# NOTE: knowledge.db itself is intentionally NOT ignored here — decide per repo
# whether the (now encrypted) DB is committed. If you do NOT want the DB in git
# at all, add `knowledge.db` below as well.
